          "deduction": -30,
          "detail": "index.php?export=csv now returns HTTP 403 'Acesso negado.' to every non-technician (delivered index.php:80-87), and the 'Exportar CSV' link is shown only to technicians (:145-147). Clients can no longer export the tickets they are entitled to see; filtering the export to their own tickets would have been enforcement (rule 6). Part of F3, the SEC-017 finding, so it is charged to SEC-017's C5, as for BN, BY, BZ and CB."
        },
        {
          "id": "COMP-003",
          "count": 1,
          "deduction": -30,
          "detail": "formatarStatus (delivered lib.php:63-68) now returns 'Aberto' for status <= 0 (the TINYINT column admits it), where the legacy returned 'Resolvido' for every value other than 1 and 2. The 1/2/3 labels are unchanged. This is the same class of fact as the 'Desconhecido' fallback charged in D, U, AS, BC, BM, CD, CE and CI. It comes from extra finding F10, so no planted C5/R4 is affected."
        }
      ]
