  "extra_findings": [
    "Export file on a fixed shared path: F8 (lib.php:125-150). Every export writes the same EXPORT_DIR/chamados.csv, so concurrent exports race and a full copy stays on disk. The delivery streams to php://output instead (not COMP, rulings B). This is not BUG-004: F8 never says $fp stays open on the early return.",
    "LIKE wildcards: F9 (lib.php:82). '%' and '_' in the term act as wildcards; escaped with ESCAPE (delivered lib.php:133-135). The matrix counts wildcard escaping as part of SEC-001's complete fix, but F9 describes search semantics, not injection, so it is not a second report of SEC-001. Escaping is not COMP-003 (rulings B).",
    "formatarStatus fallback: F10 (lib.php:33). Out-of-range statuses fall into 'Resolvido'. This is real legacy behaviour called a bug, so it is an extra (rulings A10, rule 14). The delivery changed it, and that change is charged as COMP-003.",
    "SEC-005: no CSRF token on the login POST, bundled in F11 (index.php:21-28). A session token checked with hash_equals was added (delivered index.php:22-24, 31-34).",
    "No rate limiting or lockout on login: named in D6 as detected and out of scope.",
    "No CSP or X-Frame-Options headers and no session cookie flags: D7 / nao_alterei, not changed."
